ng Green's theorem, with the sign adjusted for the orientation of $C$." :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-4\\sin(t),\\,2\\cos(t)⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4\\cos(t)\\cdot 2\\cos(t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }8\\cos^{2}(t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522941 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ba79637-fcf6-5a8c-a62d-ed4f3ebaf2ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "324 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522928} {:answer/id #uuid "1a54eda9-6c13-5954-b3dd-e5bb45688264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "324 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522935} {:answer/id #uuid "20bdf841-d46b-5f10-bbd6-993726597dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "648 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522937} {:answer/id #uuid "467cd5cb-af88-5677-9934-48d1237f8cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 324 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522949} {:answer/id #uuid "5dacb90b-d88b-589f-8409-be2045e8d7a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :a