\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}-x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨4(\\cos(t)-2\\cos(2t)),\\,3(-\\sin(t)+2\\sin(2t))⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}-x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}4(-\\sin(t)+\\sin(2t))\\cdot 3(-\\sin(t)+2\\sin(2t))\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}12(\\sin(2t)-\\sin(t))(2\\sin(2t)-\\sin(t))\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0532a3d5-8ee1-550f-b0bf-c235d929f9f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0532a3d5-8ee1-550f-b0bf-c235d929f9f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523018} :answer-field/id #uuid "02d2a19b-0275-5b3e-a499-333cc75b2412" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523017} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a169120-7df4-5f55-beae-de78fbf968d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a169120-7df4-5f55-beae-de78fbf968d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523050} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b168f6f-49e1-5695-9ee4-29603fc3f97a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4087d16f-41ff-55cd-8c2e-08b69a6826be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4087d16f-41ff-55cd-8c2e-08b69a6826be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523038} :answer-field/id #uuid "781b488a-edfc-5c44-84c9-4de420c90a9f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c01f4bfb-77a4-54f6-98c5-f72c64b9a004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c01f4bfb-77a4-54f6-98c5-f72c64b9a004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523072} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0931c90-812a-5983-b711-8c99d2ced8b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "01b49672-000e-56a4-a472-53c03786af3d" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=4\\cos(2t-\\frac{2\\pi}{3})+8,\\,y=4\\sin(2t-\\frac{2\\pi}{3})-9,\\,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le t<\\frac{5\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the normal to the curve is vertical. Give exact answers in ascending order.\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}, $t=$\n{{field-2}}, $t=$\n{{field-3}}, $t=$\n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The normal is vertical if the tangent is horizontal. Therefore, we require ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${x}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-8\\sin(2t-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=8\\cos(2t-\\frac{2\\pi}{3})\n$$\n\nSolving ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n8\\cos(2t-\\frac{2\\pi}{3})=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{7\\pi}{12}, \\frac{13\\pi}{12}, \\frac{19\\pi}{12}, \\frac{25\\pi}{12}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{12}\\right) & =-8\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{12}\\right) & =8\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{19\\pi}{12}\\right) & =-8\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{25\\pi}{12}\\right) & =8\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the normal to the curve is indeed vertical when $$\n\\displaystyle t=\\frac{7\\pi}{12}, \\frac{13\\pi}{12}, \\frac{19\\pi}{12}, \\frac{25\\pi}{12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76780c4b-7c67-5172-a923-404203abac6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523048} {:answer/id #uuid "960e68b7-6cec-5c3c-a30f-2031649d16a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{8\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523054} {:answer/id #uuid "a958f4f8-a66f-5de3-aa01-d9ebb099e2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523062} {:answer/id #uuid "eb798864-0ac9-51b0-9c7f-b01a49eef0ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523085} {:answer/id #uuid "ec200bf0-4f46-584b-a692-00c1810a50f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec200bf0-4f46-584b-a692-00c1810a50f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523086} :answer-field/id #uuid "25fc8402-d761-5db0-9a28-00207fa0223e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c0cf3c7-a877-56af-bcc4-84567b0dae9c" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\pi t)-8t,\\,y={e}^{1t},\\,0<t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the value of the parameter $t$ at which the normal line to the curve is horizontal." :question/worked-solution "The normal line is horizontal when the tangent line to the curve is vertical. Therefore, we require ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{t}-8,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=1{e}^{1t}\n$$\n\nSolving ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{t}-8=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right)=1{e}^{1\\times (1/8)}=e^{\\frac{1}{8}}\\ne 0,\\,\\,\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the normal to the curve is indeed horizontal when $t=\\frac{1}{8}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "025a69e7-e144-5e44-be3d-307e07729fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "025a69e7-e144-5e44-be3d-307e07729fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523016} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f620562-bc36-5065-97f2-e05de27b5688" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523056} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7a04206-b140-5d42-bde5-4231171751d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7a04206-b140-5d42-bde5-4231171751d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523067} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3f366e8-f2dc-5583-8eb0-e347df6aa6ab" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f7c0d8c-1437-5316-8794-8415de166fad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f7c0d8c-1437-5316-8794-8415de166fad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523057} :answer-field/id #uuid "a84c30dc-6e6a-537e-aa83-0c1014fdcbb7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ea4a20f-8288-58e3-bdf8-14dbf16d306b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea4a20f-8288-58e3-bdf8-14dbf16d306b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523033} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb4a414a-b80a-51ce-8141-525ff7e47ea3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "146bf2ed-a4b6-50b6-a118-3016f8e80fe9" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=6\\cos(2t-\\frac{3\\pi}{4})-4,\\,y=3\\sin(2t-\\frac{3\\pi}{4})-7,\\,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le t<\\frac{5\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the normal to the curve is vertical. Give exact answers in ascending order.\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}, $t=$\n{{field-2}}, $t=$\n{{field-3}}, $t=$\n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "The normal is vertical if the tangent is horizontal. Therefore, we require ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${x}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-12\\sin(2t-\\frac{3\\pi}{4}),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=6\\cos(2t-\\frac{3\\pi}{4})\n$$\n\nSolving ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n6\\cos(2t-\\frac{3\\pi}{4})=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{5\\pi}{8}, \\frac{9\\pi}{8}, \\frac{13\\pi}{8}, \\frac{17\\pi}{8}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\right) & =-12\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{9\\pi}{8}\\right) & =12\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{8}\\right) & =-12\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}\\left(\\frac{17\\pi}{8}\\right) & =12\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the normal to the curve is indeed vertical when $$\n\\displaystyle t=\\frac{5\\pi}{8}, \\frac{9\\pi}{8}, \\frac{13\\pi}{8}, \\frac{17\\pi}{8}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06494210-c8fa-5ac1-8521-fd99aa96f543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523019} {:answer/id #uuid "396110c6-534d-5443-8986-37b860b46f5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523035} {:answer/id #uuid "74b0388e-0ebf-588b-90b2-c0ea3143fd58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523046} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0e9c08-3a8b-5a43-becd-adfb70a329c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\pm \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/